Diagnostics for the Firecracker comparison's restores (PM M37, M38), against a1b501d.
Around each restore, KVM's kvm_exit, kvm_entry and kvm_userspace_exit tracepoints are
read through sudo on the trace's CLOCK_MONOTONIC. Only events before the guest's first
beat count. The summary gives time per exit reason, and a histogram of the guest RIP at
each exit. Nonzero KVM debugfs counters, shards-vm's debug log with arrival times, the
guest's mitigations and CPUID, and a per-page copy of shards' snapshot (M37) complete it.
The beat test guest here does not yet wait for the crypto self-tests (M38). On a Linux
host with KVM and passwordless sudo:

  git apply docs/research/measurements/restore-profile/diagnostics.patch
  cargo bench -p shards --bench firecracker -- --runs 20 > bench.log
  llvm-nm -n --defined-only vmlinux | awk '$2 ~ /^[TtWw]$/ {print $1, $3}' > syms.txt
  docs/research/measurements/restore-profile/profile.py syms.txt bench.log

